T'as raison, on oublie le jour de la semaine. On reste sur les requêtes simples — les mêmes qu'avant, juste avec `heure_pic_max` et `nb_sec_attention` en plus.

**7 colonnes, c'est tout :**
`date_jour | max_tps | moy_tps | min_tps | nb_depassements | heure_pic_max | nb_sec_attention`

Les requêtes sont déjà dans le fichier Excel v12 qu'on t'a envoyé — elles ont exactement ces 7 colonnes (sans `jour_semaine`). Le `CASE FROM_UNIXTIME...` n'est **pas** dans ces requêtes, il était juste dans la version du Guide.

Donc les requêtes finales à utiliser sont celles du message précédent, mais **sans le bloc `CASE ... AS jour_semaine`** :

**Requête 1s — finale :**
```sql
SELECT
    a.date_jour,
    a.max_tps,
    a.moy_tps,
    a.min_tps,
    a.nb_depassements,
    b.ts AS heure_pic_max,
    a.nb_sec_attention
FROM (
    SELECT
        SUBSTR(ts, 1, 10) AS date_jour,
        MAX(cnt) AS max_tps,
        ROUND(AVG(cnt), 1) AS moy_tps,
        MIN(cnt) AS min_tps,
        SUM(CASE WHEN cnt > 100 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS nb_depassements,
        SUM(CASE WHEN cnt > 80 AND cnt <= 100 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS nb_sec_attention
    FROM (
        SELECT
            SUBSTR(CAST(timestamp_postage_mq AS STRING), 1, 19) AS ts,
            COUNT(*) AS cnt
        FROM nom_de_ta_table
        WHERE circuit = 'RVM'
          AND timestamp_postage_mq >= '2026-03-01'
        GROUP BY SUBSTR(CAST(timestamp_postage_mq AS STRING), 1, 19)
    ) sub
    GROUP BY SUBSTR(ts, 1, 10)
) a
JOIN (
    SELECT
        SUBSTR(ts, 1, 10) AS date_jour,
        ts,
        ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY SUBSTR(ts, 1, 10) ORDER BY cnt DESC) AS rn
    FROM (
        SELECT
            SUBSTR(CAST(timestamp_postage_mq AS STRING), 1, 19) AS ts,
            COUNT(*) AS cnt
        FROM nom_de_ta_table
        WHERE circuit = 'RVM'
          AND timestamp_postage_mq >= '2026-03-01'
        GROUP BY SUBSTR(CAST(timestamp_postage_mq AS STRING), 1, 19)
    ) sub2
) b ON a.date_jour = b.date_jour AND b.rn = 1
ORDER BY a.date_jour
```

**Requête 5s — finale :**
```sql
SELECT
    a.date_jour,
    a.max_tps,
    a.moy_tps,
    a.min_tps,
    a.nb_depassements,
    CONCAT(b.hm, ':', LPAD(CAST(b.s5 AS STRING), 2, '0')) AS heure_pic_max,
    a.nb_fen_attention
FROM (
    SELECT
        SUBSTR(hm, 1, 10) AS date_jour,
        MAX(cnt5) AS max_tps,
        ROUND(AVG(cnt5), 1) AS moy_tps,
        MIN(cnt5) AS min_tps,
        SUM(CASE WHEN cnt5 > 500 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS nb_depassements,
        SUM(CASE WHEN cnt5 > 400 AND cnt5 <= 500 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS nb_fen_attention
    FROM (
        SELECT
            SUBSTR(CAST(timestamp_postage_mq AS STRING), 1, 16) AS hm,
            (CAST(SUBSTR(CAST(timestamp_postage_mq AS STRING), 18, 2) AS INT)/5)*5 AS s5,
            COUNT(*) AS cnt5
        FROM nom_de_ta_table
        WHERE circuit = 'RVM'
          AND timestamp_postage_mq >= '2026-03-01'
        GROUP BY
            SUBSTR(CAST(timestamp_postage_mq AS STRING), 1, 16),
            (CAST(SUBSTR(CAST(timestamp_postage_mq AS STRING), 18, 2) AS INT)/5)*5
    ) sub
    GROUP BY SUBSTR(hm, 1, 10)
) a
JOIN (
    SELECT
        SUBSTR(hm, 1, 10) AS date_jour,
        hm, s5,
        ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY SUBSTR(hm, 1, 10) ORDER BY cnt5 DESC) AS rn
    FROM (
        SELECT
            SUBSTR(CAST(timestamp_postage_mq AS STRING), 1, 16) AS hm,
            (CAST(SUBSTR(CAST(timestamp_postage_mq AS STRING), 18, 2) AS INT)/5)*5 AS s5,
            COUNT(*) AS cnt5
        FROM nom_de_ta_table
        WHERE circuit = 'RVM'
          AND timestamp_postage_mq >= '2026-03-01'
        GROUP BY
            SUBSTR(CAST(timestamp_postage_mq AS STRING), 1, 16),
            (CAST(SUBSTR(CAST(timestamp_postage_mq AS STRING), 18, 2) AS INT)/5)*5
    ) sub2
) b ON a.date_jour = b.date_jour AND b.rn = 1
ORDER BY a.date_jour
```

